    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d258">

                <pb facs="0386" n="214" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg214"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111M72/7</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Spain</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Willard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-31T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 31, 1917, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>376. Department’s 349, March 24, 6 p.m. Department has received further
                    information in regard to prisoners taken to Germany by auxiliary cruiser <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Moewe</hi> to the effect that at least 50 American
                    citizens are now held there. Urge the Foreign Office to obtain full report from
                    Spanish Ambassador, Berlin, as to their number, condition, and place of
                    imprisonment, and to instruct him to make every effort to secure their prompt
                    release and departure from Germany.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
